{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — css-variables

  The bridge between the Theme Editor and the token system. Phase 1 section 29.2
  specifies this snippet by name; before Phase 10 its contents sat inline in
  layout/theme.liquid.

  It emits ONE style element, after the stylesheets, carrying only the tokens a
  merchant is allowed to move. Everything else in assets/design-tokens.css stays
  developer-owned, which is what keeps the Theme Editor incapable of breaking the
  contrast system.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY THE COLOURS ARE A SCHEME AND NOT THREE PICKERS

  Phase 2 section 30 raised two guardrails and assigned both to Phase 10:

    G1  The colours cannot be free pickers. A Shopify `color` setting is
        unconstrained, and settings_schema.json has no validation hook and no
        on-save callback, so there is no mechanism to check a ratio at save
        time. A merchant nudging warm cream darker silently invalidates every
        measured pairing in the system.

    G2  A gold scheme must ship its light-surface partner. --color-accent-strong
        #82672B is a fixed hex, not computed from the gold. Changing gold alone
        left the light-surface accent behind and silently broke the pairing the
        whole system depends on — muted gold measures 1.55:1 on warm cream and
        may never carry a mark there.

  Both are answered the same way: the merchant chooses a whole SCHEME, and each
  scheme sets its dark-surface gold and its light-surface partner together, so
  the two can never desynchronise.

  Every ratio quoted below was re-measured in Phase 10 against WCAG 2.2 relative
  luminance and matches Phase 2 section 3 exactly.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE `part` PARAMETER

  The scheme has two effects on the document head and they cannot sit together:
  the theme-color meta belongs early, and the style element must come AFTER the
  stylesheets or its :root declarations lose to the ones in design-tokens.css.

  Rather than resolve the scheme twice in two places — the exact desynchronising
  that G2 exists to prevent — the snippet is rendered twice and told which part
  to emit:

    {% render 'css-variables', part: 'meta' %}    early in <head>
    {% render 'css-variables', part: 'style' %}   after the stylesheets
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    One scheme ships today: the approved brand palette. The select exists so a
    second is additive rather than a refactor, but adding one is NOT an
    engineering decision — it needs brand approval of the colour values and a
    measurement pass across the section 3 matrix. Anything less reintroduces
    exactly the risk G1 exists to remove.
  endcomment
  assign scheme = settings.color_scheme | default: 'godsquad'

  case scheme
    when 'godsquad'
      assign c_ink = '#0D0C0A'
      assign c_cream = '#F3EFE6'
      assign c_gold = '#D8C08A'
      assign c_gold_strong = '#82672B'
    else
      assign c_ink = '#0D0C0A'
      assign c_cream = '#F3EFE6'
      assign c_gold = '#D8C08A'
      assign c_gold_strong = '#82672B'
  endcase

  assign which = part | default: 'style'
-%}

{%- if which == 'meta' -%}
  <meta name="theme-color" content="{{ c_ink }}">
{%- else -%}
{% style %}
  :root {
    /* The approved palette. Measured: cream on ink 17.04:1, ink on cream
       17.04:1, gold on ink 11.01:1, gold-strong on cream 4.66:1. */
    --gs-ink: {{ c_ink }};
    --gs-cream: {{ c_cream }};
    --gs-gold: {{ c_gold }};

    /* G2. The light-surface partner travels with the gold it belongs to, in the
       same scheme, so the two cannot drift apart. */
    --gs-gold-strong: {{ c_gold_strong }};

    --container-standard: {{ settings.container_width | default: 1440 }}px;
    --radius-sm: {{ settings.radius_sm | default: 2 }}px;

    {%- comment -%}
      One ratio for the whole catalogue (Phase 2 section 27.6.5). The token
      already exists in both shapes; this picks which one every product card in
      the theme reads.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if settings.product_image_ratio == 'portrait' %}
    --product-aspect: var(--product-aspect-wide);
    {%- endif %}

    {%- if settings.type_display_font %}
    --font-display: {{ settings.type_display_font.family }}, {{ settings.type_display_font.fallback_families }};
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if settings.type_body_font %}
    --font-body: {{ settings.type_body_font.family }}, {{ settings.type_body_font.fallback_families }};
    {%- endif %}
  }
{% endstyle %}
{%- endif -%}
